Third-party components in the published container image
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The image published from this repository is a composite work. This repository's
own source is Apache-2.0, but the image also contains software that is not:

1. VerusCoin daemon (verusd, verus)
   https://github.com/VerusCoin/VerusCoin
   MIT licence. Copyright (c) 2009-2017 The Bitcoin Core developers,
   2009-2018 Bitcoin Developers, 2016-2024 The Zcash developers,
   2016-2025 The Komodo developers, 2018-2025 The VerusCoin developers.

   The binaries are downloaded unmodified from official upstream releases and
   verified against a pinned SHA-256 at build time. This project does not
   modify, patch or fork the daemon.

2. Oracle Berkeley DB 6.2.x — GNU Affero General Public License
   Upstream's COPYING states that with default build options the daemon depends
   on Berkeley DB 6.2.x, which is AGPL-licensed. The official binaries this
   image ships are built that way, so the image contains AGPL-licensed code.
   See LICENSING.md for what that means for you.

3. Debian GNU/Linux base image and its packages
   Various licences. An SPDX SBOM is attached to every release and attested to
   the image; see LICENSING.md for how to read it.

4. Zcash proving parameters
   Not shipped in the image. They are downloaded at runtime into a volume you
   own, from https://verus.io/zcparams, and hash-verified.
